@node Development
@chapter Development
@cindex development
@cindex contributing

This chapter is for developers who want to modify Codebud: run the test
suite, add a new tool, tune the planner prompt, or understand the
conventions used throughout the codebase.

@menu
* Test Suite::                  Running and understanding the tests.
* Code Style::                  Ruff configuration and formatting.
* Adding a Tool::               The five-step tool-addition checklist.
* Tuning the Planner Prompt::   Improving JSON reliability.
* Adding a Safety Rule::        Expanding or restricting what runs.
* Project Conventions::         Naming, imports, type hints, comments.
@end menu


@node Test Suite
@section Test Suite
@cindex test suite
@cindex pytest

@subsection Running the tests

@example
make check         @r{# run all tests}
make coverage      @r{# tests + branch coverage → htmlcov/}
@end example

Or invoke pytest directly for a single test:

@example
pytest tests/test_planner.py::TestRetryLogic::test_prose_first_then_valid_json_retry -v
@end example

All tests pass without a running Ollama server.  Tests that would require
network access use @code{unittest.mock.patch} to replace @code{call_llm}.

